{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/765975-deadmans-hand-backers","id":765975,"title":"Deadmans hand Backers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-14T19:03:24-08:00","id":765975,"title":"Deadmans hand Backers","content":"Who are their mysterious backers?<br /> <br /> Their almost certainly SOMEONES catspaw or deniable cutout...<br /> <br /> Question is WHOS<br /> <br /> the most obvious, and Lazyiest answer is Pentex<br /> <br /> but why would they want a militia when they have First teams...<br /> <br /> Other possibletys include... Kindred... possibly wanting to be able to distract &quot;Lupines&quot; Across the world without an attack being traced back to them.<br /> <br /> SAD say has a solitary millionaire in its ranks who quietly funded the creation of this militia to have a way to act without official scrutiny...<br /> <br /> Any other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T16:04:44-08:00","id":766607,"title":"","content":"Dead Man's Hand is a sample Pentex First Team. So I have no idea why you think there's a mystery about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T16:57:05-08:00","id":766655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/765975-deadmans-hand-backers?p=766607#post766607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dead Man's Hand is a sample Pentex First Team. So I have no idea why you think there's a mystery about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's heavily implied (paramilitary teams with anti-Garou training in an outfit that has fomor teams as well), it isn't actually spelled out.<br /> If they're meant to be a First Team, the location in the book (not near the First Teams box or even just within the Pentex part, but under the heading of &quot;other agencies&quot;) seems rather odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T17:58:14-08:00","id":766706,"title":"","content":"Dead Man's Hand first appeared in Werewolf Revised as a sample first team, but there was ambiguity as to where they came from as Revised stepped away from explicitly naming Pentex as the source of so many Werewolf woes.<br /> <br /> So short answer: Pentex backs Dead Man's Hand and similar groups.<br /> <br /> More involved answer: It's ambiguous enough it could be anything you personally want or need from your chronicle. A perfect opportunity to create a Wyrm-driven agency bent on slaughtering Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T18:00:35-08:00","id":766707,"title":"","content":"What is kind of amusing to me is that Dead Man's Hand is taken relatively straight from Revised, so characters who were active in the early-mid 90s or participated in the Falklands War in the early 80s have their histories revised so they're active in the early-mid 00s and part of Dead Man's Hand around the time of the book's publication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T00:58:26-08:00","id":766912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/765975-deadmans-hand-backers?p=766655#post766655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that's heavily implied (paramilitary teams with anti-Garou training in an outfit that has fomor teams as well), it isn't actually spelled out.<br /> If they're meant to be a First Team, the location in the book (not near the First Teams box or even just within the Pentex part, but under the heading of &quot;other agencies&quot;) seems rather odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resplendant fire got to this faster then I did. It's about First Teams not being obvious dregs of fomori villiany and Pentex emblazoned Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T01:02:16-08:00","id":766915,"title":"","content":"It's pretty easy to see how it happened that way - the Werewolf 20 antagonists chapter is mostly the Werewolf Revised antagonists chapter. One of the differences is that the Werewolf Rev chapter doesn't mention Pentex once, whereas Werewolf 20 adds an entire section about Pentex. So it's not much of a surprise that the older material (Dead Man's Hand) didn't get integrated with the newer material (Pentex).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}